// Canonical WIT for the lattice plugin host (Phase 7).
//
// Design: docs/dev/architecture/plugin-host.md §5 (the exercised-trait →
// WIT mirror). Slice sequencing: docs/dev/operations/slice-plans/plugin-host.md.
//
// One file per interface. Every interface names the native trait it mirrors
// and the slice that populates it; PH7.0 ships only the `plugin` lifecycle
// world below, wired through `wasmtime::component::bindgen!` in
// `lattice-plugin-host`. The rest are empty stubs so the package is sized
// against the full exercised set from day one (design.md §14 mitigation).
package lattice:plugin-host@0.1.0;

/// The lifecycle surface every guest component implements.
///
/// **First consumer is the user's `init.rs`** — compiled to WASM and loaded
/// by the host with a boot-capability set (CLAUDE.md tech stack; design.md
/// §5.12.2). Its `activate` runs the user's configuration: registering
/// keymaps, autocmds, hooks, and custom commands through the (stubbed here)
/// host-services / grammar / command / config / events interfaces. A plugin
/// is just another component implementing this same world with a narrower
/// capability grant; `plugins/fuzzy-finder` (PH7.4) validates the picker
/// seam but is *not* the first consumer.
///
/// The degenerate case — a component whose `activate` registers nothing — is
/// the empty `init.rs`, and is exactly what the PH7.0 scaffold instantiates
/// to prove the host round-trip end to end.
///
/// The async ABI (design.md §5.5) and the `on-event` lifecycle export land
/// with the runtime core (PH7.1) and the event seam (PH7.8) respectively;
/// PH7.0 wires the two synchronous exports needed to prove instantiation.
world plugin {
	/// Pull the shared boundary types (§4) into the world so the host gets
	/// generated Rust mirrors to round-trip against (`boundary.rs`, PH7.3a).
	/// They are not yet used by a lifecycle function signature; the `use`
	/// alone makes `bindgen!` emit them.
	use types.{args, arg-value, candidate-kind, candidate-data, raw-candidate, picker-accept-outcome};
	use types.{position, range, edit-kind, edit, edit-delta, applied-edit};
	use types.{visual-mode, selection, selection-set, visual-kind, search-direction, modal-state, register, yank-kind};
	/// The whole `effect` variant mirror + its helper types (PH7.3b1b). The
	/// multi-field payload records (`apply-edit-payload`, …) are transitively
	/// referenced by `effect`, so they surface under
	/// `crate::lattice::plugin_host::types::*` without a world-level `use`.
	use types.{effect, quit-scope, echo-level, substitute-scope, utf16-pos, lsp-request};
	/// The `app-effect` variant mirror (PH7.3b2) — the payload of the
	/// `effect::app-action` arm — plus its helper enums. `narrow-lines-payload`
	/// is transitively referenced, so it surfaces without a world-level `use`.
	use types.{app-effect, viewport-pos, scroll-pos, pane-direction, hscroll};

	/// The owned `buffer-snapshot` projection record (PH7.3c, §4.2). `use`d (not
	/// `import`ed) so `bindgen!` emits the Rust mirror the host projects into
	/// (`buffer.rs::project_buffer_snapshot`). The `document` **resource** is
	/// defined in `buffer.wit` but is not referenced by any world function yet,
	/// so bindgen won't wire it here; its host `HostDocument` trait +
	/// `add_to_linker` land at PH7.3d, when the picker-source signature takes a
	/// `document` handle (bindgen only generates a resource a signature uses).
	use buffer.{buffer-snapshot};

	/// Called once when the component is first instantiated. Runs config /
	/// contribution registration for `init.rs`; no-op for the scaffold.
	export activate: func();

	/// Called on teardown / reload (the Guard-`Drop` teardown seam, §8).
	export deactivate: func();
}
